{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/826809-amant-sacre-new-bloodline-attempt","id":826809,"title":"Amant Sacre: New Bloodline Attempt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-09T07:39:49-08:00","id":826809,"title":"Amant Sacre: New Bloodline Attempt","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Here's a very rough sketch of a bloodline I just started working on. It's based on French Escorts in the 1800s that served the nobility and kept their damned secrets. Basically escorts who were very well trusted because discretion was their brand. Anyway, having trouble with the disciplines. I'd mostly like it to be based on their own vitae and not that of others. So any help or suggestions would be greatly appreciated. Like I said, it's very rough right now. Especially the discipline. The 1st and 5th one are the only ones I've made any real progress with. The Devotion may or may not be too close to Auspex 3 and so probably will have to go.<br /> <br /> Also, I gave them a messed up bane which I really like.<br /> <br /> Amant Sacr\u00e9<br /> <b>Parent Clan</b>: Daeva</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Nicknames:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Confidants</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Bloodline Disciplines</b>: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Auspex, Majesty, Resilience, Sang Sacr\u00e9</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reputation:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Famous as trusted consorts and secret keepers, members of this bloodline often serve as companions to important and influential Kindred. Kindred trade in secrets and plots - for those who spend their entire lives withholding their machinations, nothing is more liberating than being able to trust your secrets with another soul. It is said that unburdening your soul to the Amant Sacre is the most relief some Ancient Kindred ever feel. Most Amant Sacre would suffer Final Death before revealing secrets told to them in confidence. This reputation means those of the Bloodline are greatly valued to those to whom they are close. To have an Amant Sacre as your personal consort or companion is infact considered a symbol of great status in some circles.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bloodline Gift: Sacr\u00e9d Blood</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The blood of the Amant Sacr\u00e9 is sweeter and more inviting than any others, and their Blood Bonds gain additional benefits. They are considered to have the <b>Honey Trap</b> merit. As well, they gain the <b>Beloved</b> (pg 300) and <b>Protected</b> (pg 299) merits toward anyone who has tasted their blood. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Additionally they are immune to the effects of their own blood, Amant Sacr\u00e9 do not gain blood bonds or roll for Vitae Addiction when drinking from anyone who has even a single drop of an Amant Sacr\u00e9\u2019s blood in them. Nor can they gain any sustenance from another of their Bloodline. In fact, the Amant Sacr\u00e9 almost never drink from another of their kind except in the rare cases of Diablerie.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bloodline Bane</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cursed Blood</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Though this is not a known fact, the easiest way to learn a secret from the Amant Sacr\u00e9 is to Diablerize them. This means members of this Bloodline often have a target on their backs among those few who know this flaw, especially as they grow more influential and they gather more secrets.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Further, their blood seems to call for it. Add the Amant Sacr\u00e9\u2019s dots in Sang Sacr\u00e9 as bonus dice to any Diablerie attempts made upon them, as the long-held secrets of their blood yearn to break free. While still a Breaking Point, committing Diablerie on an Amant Sacr\u00e9 restores all spent Willpower, as the Diablerist devours not just their Soul, but their entire life and memory. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a vampire reaches the third stage of Blood Bond with an Amant Sacr\u00e9 who holds a Blood Secret directly involving him, his beast tastes it in the blood and he must immediately roll to resist Frenzy with a goal of Diablerizing the Amant Sacr\u00e9. Further, Diablerizing an Amant Sacr\u00e9 always results in a</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> permanent </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Diablerie addiction toward other Amant Sacr\u00e9. For this reason they rarely keep secrets from their companions, and are quick to defend each other or investigate the murders of those in their bloodline. A Diablerist of one Amant Sacre can quickly become the Diablerist of them all.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bloodline Discipline: Sang Sacr\u00e9</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Amant Sacre know that blood holds more knowledge and power than most could ever dream of. The discipline of Sang Sacre displays the full mastery of the secrets of one\u2019s blood. However, the discipline is a double edged sword, as every use involves the tasting of vitae and risks creating addiction in the Amant Sacre, or worse, addiction in their victims, who might crave their blood to the point of violence. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blood Secret</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022) </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The keystone of the Bloodline\u2019s reputation, the Amant Sacre\u2019s blood thickens with its secrets. Users of this discipline may designate an event, memory, or piece of information a \u2018Blood Secret. A Blood Secret cannot be revealed by any mundane means, and triggers a Clash of Wills against any Discipline or other Supernatural attempts to reveal or uncover its knowledge. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Blood\u2019s Promise</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022) </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The promise of the Amant's blood means different things to different people, but an Amant is not whole if she is on her own. Above all the Amant's blood is something she shares with others. Add the Amant's dots in Sang Sacre to her Maximum Vitae. As well, When drinking from the Amant, any Vampire with Blood Potency higher than her dots in Sang Sacre receives two vitae for every one the Amant shares and is immune to the effect of Blood Bonding. This makes the Amant Sacre very attractive companions for elder Kindred who can only feed from their own kind.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Blood\u2019s Edict</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022) </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Roll: Presence + Empathy + Sang Sacre vs. Resolve + Blood Potency</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2 Vitae</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anyone who has tasted her vitae cannot speak of her Blood Secrets for their Sang Sacr\u00e9 in weeks, after which speaking of the subject requires the victim to spend a willpower and succeed on a Resolve + Composure roll with the Vampire\u2019s Sang Sacr\u00e9 as a penalty. A dramatic failure probably does something bad. A success removes the Condition which I have not created yet.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Blood's Vengeance </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) </span></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Vitae<br /> <b>Roll</b>: Resolve + Empathy + Sang Sacre vs. Resolve + Blood Potency<br /> Duration: 1 Scene<br /> For the Amant Sacre, sharing blood is an act of trust. Their blood is not something to be taken by violence, but given freely. Those who would try to inflict their desire upon an Amant by force soon find themselves in for a rude awakening as the blood boils in their mouth and body. This is the Amant's primary defense against would-be Diablerists, as well as Elders who might come hunting for the Amant for vitae.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: Something bad.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Nothing. Sorry you're gonna die.<br /> <b>Success</b>: For the remainder of the scene, any Kindred who causes lethal damage to the Amant suffers her blood's vengeance.The blood burns like fire in the assailant's mouth and body, dealing 1 point of lethal damage for every point of Vitae that vampire has ingested or ingests for the duration.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Something good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tame the Blood\u2019s Beast </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Vitae</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Amant Sacre\u2019s blood can tame the Beasts of even the most monstrous Kindred. Any Kindred who tastes the blood of an Amant Sacre with this discipline suffers their dots in Sang Sacre to all Discipline, Lashing Out and Clash of Will rolls against any member of this Bloodline. Further, once per day they may immediately end frenzy or incite frenzy in the vampire (with terms set by the Amant Sacre).</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Bloodline Devotions</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Blood\u2019s Revelation</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Auspex 1, Sang Sacre 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A creature\u2019s life is retained in its blood. This Discipline steals the memories from the subject's mind, ripping them in scattered shards and allowing the user to recall events as they happened to the victim. Though the process is painless for the victim and the victim retains her memory, some victims will experience momentary disorientation if they try to remember any of the memories that have been &quot;stolen.&quot; </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The user must have tasted (and swallowed) some of the subject's blood within the last hour. If he has done so, the werewolf is able to meditate on the act of consuming another creature's blood and unlock the secrets of the victim's life. The Uratha can access a store of the subject's memories, which are now within his own mind. It is confusing at first, though the werewolf is always aware that the events &quot;never happened to him,&quot; as such. Storytellers should feel free to describe the chaotic nature of the memories that come in a broken stream of information.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Basic notes I'm trying to hit: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Based on the private French escorts of the 1800s who served kings and kept their secrets. Famous for being able to keep secrets, trusted among Kindred. Considered a status symbol to have one as your companion. Often very beloved by their companions due to that sweet sweet vitae. Once you diablerize them you get every memory they ever had, including knowing that diablerie is the best way to get the secrets of others of their kind. Bonuses to diablerizing them. Also permanently become addicted to diablerizing the bloodline if you ever do it. Their blood is great and good at keeping secrets.They always investigate suspicious deaths of their kind and violently hunt down Kindred who diablerize one, because of the permanent addiction. Anyone who does it will definitely hunt down their bloodline forever. Very close knit.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 02-10-2016, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T07:52:56-08:00","id":826820,"title":"","content":"Also i posted this right before i ran off for work, so im only just now noticing the format is Shiite. Will fix when i get back","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T08:44:01-08:00","id":826851,"title":"","content":"My first gut-thought was &quot;if discretion is supposed to be one of their strong suits, why do they have Auspex instead of Obfuscate?&quot; But their discretion is a matter of <i>character</i>, not their talents, and that gives them a strong identity that is supported by what they can do instead of leaning on it.<br /> <br /> Their circumstances seem... really hazardous to their survival as a known bloodline, considering how kindred tend to be about their secrets. If anything, they give me something of a 'confessor' vibe rather than confidant, but that may be my Lancea Et Sanctum bias talking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-09-2016, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:33:55-08:00","id":826885,"title":"","content":"Why would Kindred want to tell them their secrets in the first place? What do they gain? We know their Blood makes Kindred feel good and makes them feel protective of the Amant, but what do the Amant actually do for them?<br /> <br /> Example of one possible direction: That their Vitae is extra-nourishing for elders, and/or <i>doesn't actually cause a blood bond</i>. That might incentivize a BP6 Elder to keep an Amant around to feed on them. Maybe it doesn't actually blood-bond people, but does make them more inclined to protect the Amant too. That the Amant learns their secrets could be either a property of the feeding process on them or a product of deliberate power usage, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:43:38-08:00","id":826892,"title":"","content":"I agree that other vampires need stronger motivators to actually trust or rely on them. Their cultural role is interesting, but it clashes with some things about vampire relations that are just a given, and their powers do paint a target on their backs more than help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T21:16:42-08:00","id":827300,"title":"","content":"I added a bunch of stuff and hopefully made the thing more readable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/826809-amant-sacre-new-bloodline-attempt?p=826885#post826885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would Kindred want to tell them their secrets in the first place? What do they gain? We know their Blood makes Kindred feel good and makes them feel protective of the Amant, but what do the Amant actually do for them?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I guess my thought behind that was the fact that they can't keep secrets from people who drink from their blood (or risk a frenzied diablerie) means that you can have a Kindred companion that you can trust implicitly, which is very very rare in the world of Vampire. But I guess that's sort of the roles Ghouls play. Someone you can trust because they're dependent on you. Maybe it was a bit naive of me to think that a trustworthy companion and a real relationship would be valuable to Kindred.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/826809-amant-sacre-new-bloodline-attempt?p=826885#post826885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example of one possible direction: That their Vitae is extra-nourishing for elders, and/or <i>doesn't actually cause a blood bond</i>. That might incentivize a BP6 Elder to keep an Amant around to feed on them. Maybe it doesn't actually blood-bond people, but does make them more inclined to protect the Amant too. That the Amant learns their secrets could be either a property of the feeding process on them or a product of deliberate power usage, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. I updated the second dot to add something to that effect. Good idea, thanks. Makes a lot more sense and makes them very valuable to the right people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/826809-amant-sacre-new-bloodline-attempt?p=826851#post826851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their circumstances seem... really hazardous to their survival as a known bloodline, considering how kindred tend to be about their secrets. If anything, they give me something of a 'confessor' vibe rather than confidant, but that may be my Lancea Et Sanctum bias talking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the part under Reputation is what's known about the Bloodline, the diablerie stuff wouldn't exactly be public knowledge and is probably something they would guard carefully. I think only someone who's Diablerized a member of the bloodline, as well as the Amant themselves would have that knowledge. Maybe some Scholar of Bloodlines as you said, probably from the Lancea or something would know as well, but definitely not common knowledge.<br /> <br /> Mostly just their general reputation, and the fact that they can be trusted to keep secrets, as well as maybe now the fact that their blood doesn't bond Elders would be known outright.<br /> <br /> And yeah, it is a really tricky task surviving as one of the Amant, which is sort of what I was hoping for. Sort a tightrope of managing secrets and relationships, of making yourself invaluable to the right person or finding the right companion or elder to protect you. They have the reputation of their bloodline as something they have to wield carefully and leverage to the right people at the right times. Not that they're necessarily terribly manipulative, but it does require a lot of finesse to survive when your blood tempts diablerie as theirs does. That's what I was thinking anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}